{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"581f45644d92803ae8652802eb862b4a313c03ba3a4d2e7508d07c24e6dd4b6b","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-plan gate / code-reading gates","key_entities":["rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle","rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha","rebar._build_info.COMMIT","hatch_build.py","/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","rebar.toml"],"problem_keywords":["gate run","build drift","stale build","base ref","code-reading gate","config mismatch","version skew"],"propositions":["A gate run snapshots the base ref tree but does not warn when the running build binary is older than the pinned base ref commit.","A stale build silently reviews new material with outdated code, causing config keys from newer commits to be unrecognized and ignored.","The running build's commit can be resolved via _gate_commit_sha() or the baked COMMIT value, enabling drift detection by checking ancestry in the target repo.","When build commit is a strict ancestor of the pinned sha, exactly one warning must be emitted with build sha, commit date, pinned sha, and drift count without altering verdict or exit code."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787714738832919001,"uuid":"4aa2e3d1-f75e-4e4a-b865-44b2794f57a6"}